CORE JAVA NOTES
=================

1. What is Java?

Java is a high-level, object-oriented, platform-independent programming language.

Features:

Platform independent

Object-oriented

Secure

Robust

Multithreaded

Automatic memory management

JDK vs JRE vs JVM

Term

Meaning

JDK

Java Development Kit – tools to develop Java applications

JRE

Java Runtime Environment – libraries and runtime components

JVM

Java Virtual Machine – executes Java bytecode

Flow:

Java Source Code (.java) → Compiler (javac) → Bytecode (.class) → JVM → Machine Code

2. OOP Concepts

Encapsulation

Wrapping data and methods into a single class and controlling access using access modifiers.

Example:

public class Employee {
    private String name;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}


